a widget on a non-existent page would likely fail or cause errors. I should:\n1. Inform the user that the page \"missing_panel\" doesn't exist\n2. Ask if they want to create the page first, or if there's a typo in the page name\n\nI should not proceed with the widget creation since the page doesn't exist. This follows the behavior principle #4: \"若信息不足,先调用查询类工具或向用户确认\" (If information is insufficient, first call query tools or confirm with the user).\n\nLet me respond to the user explaining the situation."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 10, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 3276, "output_tokens": 360, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 14295.429499999955}, "judge": null}
