o-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3462, "output_tokens": 364, "latency_ms": 7318.177399982233, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我现在处于 CONFIG_ALARM 阶段，可用的工具是 manage_alarms、manage_databases、manage_schedules 和 manage_graphics。用户要求给 TI-201 设置 HH alarm 和 LL alarm，分别在 100 和 10，priority 设为 high。\n\n首先，我需要确认 TI-201 这个点位是否存在，以及它的类型。但是，我目前没有 manage_points 工具可用。根据行为准则，如果信息不足，我应该先调用查询类工具或向用户确认。然而，在当前阶段，我没有查询点位的工具。也许我可以直接尝试创建报警，但如果点位不存在，可能会失败。不过，我可以假设 TI-201 是一个模拟量点位，因为 HH 和 LL 通常用于模拟量。\n\n让我使用 manage_alarms 来创建两个模拟量报警：一个 HH 报警（高限为 100），一个 LL 报警（低限为 10）。我需要为每个报警指定一个唯一的 ID。例如，HH 报警可以命名为 \"alarm_TI201_HH\"，LL 报警命名为 \"alarm_TI201_LL\"。优先级都设为 high。\n\n首先，创建 HH 报警。"}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3900, "output_tokens": 223, "latency_ms": 5184.236500004772, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要创建两个报警：HH报警（高限100）和LL报警（低限10）。工具要求提供id、tag、action，以及high_limit、low_limit、deadband和priority。对于HH报警，high_limit=100，low_limit设为null。对于LL报警，low_limit=10，high_limit设为null。但错误显示low_limit应该是数字，不能解析字符串。我传入了None，但在JSON中可能是null。让我尝试省略low_limit参数，使用默认值null。或者明确设置为null。在JSON中，null是有效的。让我再试一次。"}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4197, "output_tokens": 252, "latency_ms": 5679.924600000959, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "让我仔细看一下工具的schema。create_analog_alarm参数中，high_limit和low_limit的类型是\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]，并且默认值是null。但错误信息说\"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"，这可能意味着当我不提供参数时，系统尝试将空值解析为数字。也许我需要明确提供low_limit为null。在JSON中，null是有效的。让我尝试显式设置low_limit为null。在工具调用中，我需要以JSON格式提供参数。在manage_alarms函数中，参数是JSON对象。我应该提供low_limit: null。让我再试一次。"}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4523, "output_tokens": 172, "latency_ms": 4073.333599983016, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要直接传入数字和null，而不是字符串。让我用正确的JSON格式。low_limit应该是null或数字，而不是字符串\"None\"。在参数中，我应该使用数值和null。让我重新构造。对于HH报警，low_limit应该是null。对于LL报警，high_limit应该是null。现在创建HH报警：low_limit设置为null。"}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4769, "output_tokens": 200, "latency_ms": 4478.136099991389, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我遇到了参数传递的问题。在JSON中，null应该直接写为null而不是字符串\"None\"。让我仔细检查工具的JSON Schema。manage_alarms工具的参数定义中，high_limit和low_limit的类型是\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]，默认值是null。在JSON中，null是一个有效的值，我应该直接使用null而不是字符串\"None\"。让我再试一次，这次直接使用null作为值。"}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5043, "output_tokens": 349, "latency_ms": 7131.241700000828, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我需要只传入必需参数和实际需要的参数。让我重新尝试，只传入必需参数和需要的限值：", "reasoning": "The user wants me to create HH and LL alarms for tag TI-201. The issue is that when I don't pass the low_limit or pass \"None\" as a string, it's failing. Let me try without including low_limit at all - since it has a default of null, it should work if I simply don't include it in the parameters.\n\nWait, I've been trying that. Let me look at the schema more carefully:\n\n```\n\"high_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"High Limit\"},\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"},\n```\n\nThe issue might be that when I don't include the parameter but still pass it as part of the function call, it gets serialized incorrectly. Let me try a cleaner approach - only pass the required parameters plus the ones I actually need.\n\nFor HH alarm: only need high_limit = 100\nFor LL alarm: only need low_limit = 10\n\nLet me try again with minimal parameters."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5466, "output_tokens": 438, "latency_ms": 10826.770699990448, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我遇到了参数格式问题。让我换一种方式尝试，只传入必需参数和明确的数值参数：", "reasoning": "I'm having trouble with the tool calls. The error message says \"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\". It seems like when I don't include low_limit, it might be getting a default value that's not a number or null properly.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe I need to explicitly set both limits, and for HH alarm set low_limit to null explicitly in the JSON. But looking at the tool definition, it shows `\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}`. So null should be acceptable.\n\nThe issue might be that my parameter syntax is wrong. In JSON, null is represented as `null`, not `\"None\"`. Let me try with the actual JSON null value.\n\nActually, looking at my attempts, I've been using `\"None\"` as a string, not actual null. In the parameter XML, I need to represent null properly. But the function expects JSON parameters... Let me think about this differently.\n\nLooking at the tool schema again:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}\n```\n\nThe default is null, so if I don't include it, it should default to null. But I'm still getting an error. Maybe there's a bug in the system, or maybe I need to explicitly pass null.\n\nLet me try again with just the required parameters and high_limit for HH, and see if the system can handle the default null value."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 10, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 35804, "output_tokens": 2511, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 60850.82130000228}, "judge": null}
